        <p>BIRTHS, MARRIAGES, DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Notices it births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in "The Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, is. 6d. each; every additional seven words, 6d.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-11-20_WidnesExaminer_art0089" n="art0089">
        <head>Marriages.</head>
        <p>Marriages.</p>
        <p>SIDDALL.—WILLIAMS. November 13th, at Cairo-street Chapel Alfred Edward, only son of • the late Mr. and Mrs. James Siddall, of Cheater, to Lucy. daughter of Edward Williams, 4, Thynne- • street, Warrinzton.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-11-20_WidnesExaminer_art0090" n="art0090">
        <head>Deaths.</head>
        <p>Deaths.</p>
        <p>IRVING.—At her residence, The Redlands. Robert- son street, Greenock, on the 18th inst., Eliza Harriet (Lillie) Irving, widow of Thomas Irving, and daughter of the late Wm. Savage, Registrar, Warrington Cemetery.</p>
        <p>WALKER.—On 13th November, .at the Ship Inn Liverpool-road, Sarah Walker, aged 70 years.</p>
        <p>In Memoriam.</p>
        <p>MESSITER.—In loving memory of our dear father, George Malem liessiter, who died November 23rd, 1914.</p>
        <p>Sadly missed by WIFE and FAMILY. 27, Rolleston-Street, Warrington. TAYLOR.—In loving memory of Thomas Preston Taylor, who died November 16th, 1914. Tune has not dimmed our thoughts; Thoughts dwell where they seldom are seen. SONS and DAUGHTERS.</p>
      </div>
